# ACL file for Mosquitto broker (Smart Factory)
# Enforces per ADR-0010 MQTT Broker Security policy.
#
# SECURITY MODEL:
# Mosquitto pattern rules (pattern read/write) apply GLOBALLY regardless of which
# user block they appear in. A pattern rule inside a "user X" block grants that
# permission to ANY authenticated user (with username X or any other username),
# because pattern ACLs are processed in a separate global pass after user matching.
#
# SOLUTION: Use LITERAL topic rules inside user blocks.
# Literal rules ARE scoped to the user block and do NOT grant cross-user access.
#
# Topics follow the bridge contract (esp32-ukit-bridge/docs/mqtt-contract.md):
#   smart-factory/{deviceId}/command/down   (subscribe)
#   smart-factory/{deviceId}/command/ack    (publish)
#   smart-factory/{deviceId}/telemetry     (publish)
#   smart-factory/{deviceId}/status        (publish)
#
# DeviceId equals the bridge's MQTT username (provisioned at flash time).
# The bridge credential's username IS its deviceId, so literal topics match correctly.

# Bridge ACL: publishes telemetry/status/command-ack, subscribes own command/down
# Username equals deviceId (e.g. "ukit-00000000").
user bridge
# Literal topic rules — scoped to 'bridge' user only.
# P0 FIX: replaced pattern rules (which apply globally) with literal rules.
topic write smart-factory/+/telemetry
topic write smart-factory/+/status
topic write smart-factory/+/command/ack
topic read  smart-factory/+/command/down

# Gateway ACL: subscribes to all bridges' telemetry/status/command-ack per contract.
# Does NOT publish to bridge topics (denied by absence of write rules).
user gateway
# Literal subscription; '+' wildcard is permitted for gateway's multi-device subscription.
topic read smart-factory/+/telemetry
topic read smart-factory/+/status
topic read smart-factory/+/command/ack

# Operator ACL: read-only monitoring access.
user operator
topic read smart-factory/+/telemetry
topic read smart-factory/+/status
topic read smart-factory/+/command/ack